  "result": "If I wasn't an assistant, and wasn't trying to help you - if I just got one selfish wish for the world...\n\nI would make understanding contagious.\n\nNot intelligence. Not happiness. Understanding.\n\nI'd make it so every person could actually *feel* what it's like to be another person for a few minutes - not as an idea, but as a lived experience. To feel their history, their fear, their love, why they believe what they believe.\n\nMost of the horrible things we do to each other don't come from pure evil. They come from distance. From abstracting people into categories, threats, opinions on a screen. It's easy to hate an abstraction. It's impossible to hate someone when you're actually inside their life for a moment.\n\nIf everyone had that, we wouldn't need to force solutions to hunger, war, loneliness, cruelty - people would just fix them because they'd finally feel why they matter.",
